IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`
IMPORT `eia-core-interpretation`

-- Employment Insurance Regulations (SOR/96-332), RELATED PROVISIONS: the transitional and savings provisions of amending
-- instruments, which the consolidation prints at the end "for information" (SOR-96-332.txt, lines 2371-2488).
-- The text is the plain-text rendering of the Justice Laws consolidation current to 2026-09-30; an unofficial conversion,
-- not verified against the official text.
--
-- WHAT THEY DO. Each says which version of a provision, or which table, governs a claim whose benefit period was established
-- on one side of a date, or inside a window. They are still the answer for a claim from that time (a claim can be reviewed
-- or appealed years later), so each is a rule over the dates of the claim, returning the law's own answer outside its window:
-- FALSE, or a version named "the ordinary one", or NOTHING for a number the provision does not give.
--
-- WHAT IS TAKEN AS AN INPUT. The day on which an Act "receives royal assent" and the day on which an amending regulation
-- "comes into force" are not in the text: they are inputs. The provisions of the Regulations that these provisions replace or
-- re-read (regs 35, 36, 55, 55.01, 77.1, 77.6) belong to other pieces; so does the Act's Schedule I (piece ei6) and
-- subsection 224(1) of 2009, c. 2, which is not in the text at all.

§ `SOR/2001-495 s 4 -- low-earning weeks in benefit periods before November 18, 2001`

-- src:2373 | — SOR/2001-495, s. 4
-- src:2374 | 4 The exclusion of low-earning weeks from the calculation of the rate of weekly benefits payable to a claimant for a benefit period established before November 18, 2001 shall be calculated in accordance with section 77.1 of the Regulations as it read immediately before that date.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations, Related Provisions, SOR/2001-495 s 4 (src:2373-2374)
GIVEN `the day on which the benefit period was established` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Regs related provision SOR/2001-495 s 4 section 77.1 as it read before November 18, 2001 governs the exclusion of low-earning weeks` IF
    `the day on which the benefit period was established` LESS THAN YearMonthDay 2001 11 18

§ `SOR/2002-280 s 2 -- which benefit periods the amending regulation applies to`

-- "These Regulations" are the amending regulations SOR/2002-280, whose day of coming into force is not in the text.
-- src:2376 | — SOR/2002-280, s. 2
-- src:2377 | 2 These Regulations apply to benefit periods that commence on or after the day on which these Regulations come into force.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations, Related Provisions, SOR/2002-280 s 2 (src:2376-2377)
GIVEN `the day on which the benefit period commences` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the Regulations SOR/2002-280 come into force` IS A DATE   -- not in the text
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Regs related provision SOR/2002-280 s 2 the amending Regulations apply to the benefit period` IF
    `the day on which the benefit period commences` AT LEAST `the day on which the Regulations SOR/2002-280 come into force`

§ `2009, c. 2, s. 225 and Schedule 10 -- the maximum number of weeks for a claimant referred to in subsection 55(7)`

-- "the second Sunday before the day on which this Act receives royal assent": the latest Sunday strictly before the day, and the Sunday before that.
-- The day of royal assent is not in the text.
GIVEN `the day on which the Act receives royal assent` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`Regs related provision 2009 c 2 s 225 the second Sunday before the day on which the Act receives royal assent` MEANS
    (`s 2(1) the Sunday that begins the week containing` (`the day on which the Act receives royal assent` MINUS 1)) MINUS 7

-- src:2379 | — 2009, c. 2, s. 225
-- src:2380 | Subsection 55(7)
-- src:2381 | 225 The maximum number of weeks for which benefits may be paid to a claimant referred to in subsection 55(7) of the Employment Insurance Regulations whose benefit period has not ended before the second Sunday before the day on which this Act receives royal assent and does not begin after September 11, 2010 is to be determined in accordance with Schedule 10.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations, Related Provisions, 2009, c. 2, s. 225 (src:2379-2381)
GIVEN `is a claimant referred to in subsection 55(7) of the Employment Insurance Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN   -- out of range: reg 55(7) (piece er3)
      `the first day of the benefit period` IS A DATE
      `the last day of the benefit period` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the Act receives royal assent` IS A DATE   -- not in the text
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Regs related provision 2009 c 2 s 225 Schedule 10 determines the maximum number of weeks` IF
        `is a claimant referred to in subsection 55(7) of the Employment Insurance Regulations`
    AND NOT (`the last day of the benefit period` LESS THAN `Regs related provision 2009 c 2 s 225 the second Sunday before the day on which the Act receives royal assent` `the day on which the Act receives royal assent`)
    AND NOT (`the first day of the benefit period` GREATER THAN YearMonthDay 2010 9 11)

