§ `2009, c. 2, s. 226 -- Pilot Project No. 10`

-- (1) "deemed to cease to have effect on the second Saturday before the day on which this Act receives royal assent": the latest Saturday
-- strictly before that day is the day before the Sunday that begins its week, and the second is a week earlier.
-- src:2428 | — 2009, c. 2, s. 226
-- src:2429 | Pilot Project No. 10
-- src:2430 | 226 (1) Section 77.6 of the Employment Insurance Regulations is deemed to cease to have effect on the second Saturday before the day on which this Act receives royal assent.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations, Related Provisions, 2009, c. 2, s. 226(1) (src:2428-2430)
GIVEN `the day on which the Act receives royal assent` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`Regs related provision 2009 c 2 s 226(1) the day on which section 77.6 is deemed to cease to have effect` MEANS
    (`s 2(1) the Sunday that begins the week containing` `the day on which the Act receives royal assent`) MINUS 8

-- src:2431 | Transitional
-- src:2432 | (2) The maximum number of weeks for which benefits may be paid in a benefit period that is established for a claimant who is included in Pilot Project No. 10 and whose benefit period has not ended before the second Sunday before the day on which this Act receives royal assent is to be determined in accordance with Schedule I to the Employment Insurance Act, as enacted by subsection 224(1).
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations, Related Provisions, 2009, c. 2, s. 226(2) (src:2431-2432)
GIVEN `is included in Pilot Project No. 10` IS A BOOLEAN   -- out of range: reg 77.6, since repealed (piece er5)
      `the last day of the benefit period` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the Act receives royal assent` IS A DATE   -- not in the text
      `the maximum number of weeks that Schedule I to the Employment Insurance Act as enacted by subsection 224(1) gives` IS A NUMBER   -- out of range: the Act's Schedule I (piece ei6); subsection 224(1) of 2009, c. 2 is not in the text
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Regs related provision 2009 c 2 s 226(2) the maximum number of weeks for which benefits may be paid` IS
    IF     `is included in Pilot Project No. 10`
       AND NOT (`the last day of the benefit period` LESS THAN `Regs related provision 2009 c 2 s 225 the second Sunday before the day on which the Act receives royal assent` `the day on which the Act receives royal assent`)
    THEN JUST `the maximum number of weeks that Schedule I to the Employment Insurance Act as enacted by subsection 224(1) gives`
    ELSE NOTHING

§ `2009, c. 30, ss. 3 to 7 -- more weeks for claimants referred to in subsection 55(7) with a record of contributions`

-- "contributed at least 30% of the maximum annual employee's premium in 7 of the 10 years before the beginning of the claimant's benefit period":
-- the count is of years, among the n years before the benefit period, in which the claimant contributed at least that. Read as "at least 7 of the 10"
-- (fork F-30-ATLEAST in NOTES.md). The person states the six counts.
DECLARE `er6 Years of contribution before the benefit period` HAS
    `years among the 10 years before in which the claimant contributed at least 30% of the maximum annual employee’s premium` IS A NUMBER
    `years among the 11 years before in which the claimant contributed at least 30% of the maximum annual employee’s premium` IS A NUMBER
    `years among the 12 years before in which the claimant contributed at least 30% of the maximum annual employee’s premium` IS A NUMBER
    `years among the 13 years before in which the claimant contributed at least 30% of the maximum annual employee’s premium` IS A NUMBER
    `years among the 14 years before in which the claimant contributed at least 30% of the maximum annual employee’s premium` IS A NUMBER
    `years among the 15 years before in which the claimant contributed at least 30% of the maximum annual employee’s premium` IS A NUMBER

-- s 3: a benefit period established from January 4, 2009 to June 5, 2010
-- src:2434 | — 2009, c. 30, s. 3
-- src:2435 | Subsection 55(7) of regulations
-- src:2436 | 3 Despite section 225 of the Budget Implementation Act, 2009, if a claimant is a claimant referred to in subsection 55(7) of the Employment Insurance Regulations who was paid less than 36 weeks of regular benefits in the 260 weeks before the beginning of the claimant’s benefit period and that benefit period was established during the period that begins on January 4, 2009 and ends on June 5, 2010, the number of weeks of benefits in Schedule 10 to that Act that apply in respect of that claimant is deemed to be the number of weeks that would otherwise apply in respect of the claimant but for this section increased by
-- src:2437 | (a) 5 weeks, if the claimant contributed at least 30% of the maximum annual employee’s premium in 7 of the 10 years before the beginning of the claimant’s benefit period;
-- src:2438 | (b) 8 weeks, if the claimant contributed at least 30% of the maximum annual employee’s premium in 8 of the 11 years before the beginning of the claimant’s benefit period;
-- src:2439 | (c) 11 weeks, if the claimant contributed at least 30% of the maximum annual employee’s premium in 9 of the 12 years before the beginning of the claimant’s benefit period;
-- src:2440 | (d) 14 weeks, if the claimant contributed at least 30% of the maximum annual employee’s premium in 10 of the 13 years before the beginning of the claimant’s benefit period;
-- src:2441 | (e) 17 weeks, if the claimant contributed at least 30% of the maximum annual employee’s premium in 11 of the 14 years before the beginning of the claimant’s benefit period; or
-- src:2442 | (f) 20 weeks, if the claimant contributed at least 30% of the maximum annual employee’s premium in at least 12 of the 15 years before the beginning of the claimant’s benefit period.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations, Related Provisions, 2009, c. 30, s. 3 (src:2434-2442)
GIVEN `is a claimant referred to in subsection 55(7) of the Employment Insurance Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `weeks of regular benefits paid in the 260 weeks before the beginning of the benefit period` IS A NUMBER
      `the day on which the benefit period was established` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Regs related provision 2009 c 30 s 3 the section applies to the claimant` IF
        `is a claimant referred to in subsection 55(7) of the Employment Insurance Regulations`
    AND `weeks of regular benefits paid in the 260 weeks before the beginning of the benefit period` LESS THAN 36
    AND `the day on which the benefit period was established` AT LEAST YearMonthDay 2009 1 4
    AND `the day on which the benefit period was established` AT MOST YearMonthDay 2010 6 5

-- The paragraphs are alternatives with larger and larger increases; when more than one is met the largest applies (fork F-30-LARGEST).
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations, Related Provisions, 2009, c. 30, s. 3 (src:2437-2442)
GIVEN years IS AN `er6 Years of contribution before the benefit period`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Regs related provision 2009 c 30 s 3 the increase in the number of weeks` IS
    BRANCH IF years's `years among the 15 years before in which the claimant contributed at least 30% of the maximum annual employee’s premium` AT LEAST 12 THEN 20   -- (f)
           IF years's `years among the 14 years before in which the claimant contributed at least 30% of the maximum annual employee’s premium` AT LEAST 11 THEN 17   -- (e)
           IF years's `years among the 13 years before in which the claimant contributed at least 30% of the maximum annual employee’s premium` AT LEAST 10 THEN 14   -- (d)
           IF years's `years among the 12 years before in which the claimant contributed at least 30% of the maximum annual employee’s premium` AT LEAST 9 THEN 11   -- (c)
           IF years's `years among the 11 years before in which the claimant contributed at least 30% of the maximum annual employee’s premium` AT LEAST 8 THEN 8   -- (b)
           IF years's `years among the 10 years before in which the claimant contributed at least 30% of the maximum annual employee’s premium` AT LEAST 7 THEN 5   -- (a)
           OTHERWISE 0

@ref Employment Insurance Regulations, Related Provisions, 2009, c. 30, s. 3 (src:2434-2442)
GIVEN `is a claimant referred to in subsection 55(7) of the Employment Insurance Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `weeks of regular benefits paid in the 260 weeks before the beginning of the benefit period` IS A NUMBER
      `the day on which the benefit period was established` IS A DATE
      years IS AN `er6 Years of contribution before the benefit period`
      `the number of weeks that would otherwise apply` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Regs related provision 2009 c 30 s 3 the number of weeks of benefits deemed to apply` IS
    IF `Regs related provision 2009 c 30 s 3 the section applies to the claimant` `is a claimant referred to in subsection 55(7) of the Employment Insurance Regulations` `weeks of regular benefits paid in the 260 weeks before the beginning of the benefit period` `the day on which the benefit period was established`
    THEN JUST (`the number of weeks that would otherwise apply` PLUS `Regs related provision 2009 c 30 s 3 the increase in the number of weeks` years)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- s 4: a benefit period established from June 6, 2010 to July 10, 2010
