      `the number of weeks that would otherwise apply` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Regs related provision 2009 c 30 s 5 the number of weeks of benefits deemed to apply` IS
    IF `Regs related provision 2009 c 30 s 5 the section applies to the claimant` `is a claimant referred to in subsection 55(7) of the Employment Insurance Regulations` `weeks of regular benefits paid in the 260 weeks before the beginning of the benefit period` `the day on which the benefit period was established`
    THEN JUST (`the number of weeks that would otherwise apply` PLUS `Regs related provision 2009 c 30 s 5 the increase in the number of weeks` years)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- s 6: a benefit period established from August 8, 2010 to September 11, 2010
-- src:2461 | — 2009, c. 30, s. 6
-- src:2462 | Subsection 55(7) of regulations
-- src:2463 | 6 Despite section 225 of the Budget Implementation Act, 2009, if a claimant is a claimant referred to in subsection 55(7) of the Employment Insurance Regulations who was paid less than 36 weeks of regular benefits in the 260 weeks before the beginning of the claimant’s benefit period and that benefit period was established during the period that begins on August 8, 2010 and ends on September 11, 2010, the number of weeks of benefits in Schedule 10 to that Act that apply in respect of that claimant is deemed to be the number of weeks that would otherwise apply in respect of the claimant but for this section increased by
-- src:2464 | (a) 2 weeks, if the claimant contributed at least 30% of the maximum annual employee’s premium in 11 of the 14 years before the beginning of the claimant’s benefit period; or
-- src:2465 | (b) 5 weeks, if the claimant contributed at least 30% of the maximum annual employee’s premium in at least 12 of the 15 years before the beginning of the claimant’s benefit period.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations, Related Provisions, 2009, c. 30, s. 6 (src:2461-2465)
GIVEN `is a claimant referred to in subsection 55(7) of the Employment Insurance Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `weeks of regular benefits paid in the 260 weeks before the beginning of the benefit period` IS A NUMBER
      `the day on which the benefit period was established` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Regs related provision 2009 c 30 s 6 the section applies to the claimant` IF
        `is a claimant referred to in subsection 55(7) of the Employment Insurance Regulations`
    AND `weeks of regular benefits paid in the 260 weeks before the beginning of the benefit period` LESS THAN 36
    AND `the day on which the benefit period was established` AT LEAST YearMonthDay 2010 8 8
    AND `the day on which the benefit period was established` AT MOST YearMonthDay 2010 9 11

@ref Employment Insurance Regulations, Related Provisions, 2009, c. 30, s. 6 (src:2464-2465)
GIVEN years IS AN `er6 Years of contribution before the benefit period`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Regs related provision 2009 c 30 s 6 the increase in the number of weeks` IS
    BRANCH IF years's `years among the 15 years before in which the claimant contributed at least 30% of the maximum annual employee’s premium` AT LEAST 12 THEN 5   -- (b)
           IF years's `years among the 14 years before in which the claimant contributed at least 30% of the maximum annual employee’s premium` AT LEAST 11 THEN 2   -- (a)
           OTHERWISE 0

@ref Employment Insurance Regulations, Related Provisions, 2009, c. 30, s. 6 (src:2461-2465)
GIVEN `is a claimant referred to in subsection 55(7) of the Employment Insurance Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `weeks of regular benefits paid in the 260 weeks before the beginning of the benefit period` IS A NUMBER
      `the day on which the benefit period was established` IS A DATE
      years IS AN `er6 Years of contribution before the benefit period`
      `the number of weeks that would otherwise apply` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Regs related provision 2009 c 30 s 6 the number of weeks of benefits deemed to apply` IS
    IF `Regs related provision 2009 c 30 s 6 the section applies to the claimant` `is a claimant referred to in subsection 55(7) of the Employment Insurance Regulations` `weeks of regular benefits paid in the 260 weeks before the beginning of the benefit period` `the day on which the benefit period was established`
    THEN JUST (`the number of weeks that would otherwise apply` PLUS `Regs related provision 2009 c 30 s 6 the increase in the number of weeks` years)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- s 7: "With respect to a claimant to whom any of sections 3 to 6 applies whose benefit period has not been extended under any of
-- subsections 10(13) to (13.3)": subsection 55(10) is deemed to read that the total of combined weeks "shall not exceed 50 or, if the
-- maximum number of weeks ... under section 225 ... is equal to or greater than 50 weeks as a result of the application of any provision of any
-- Act of Parliament, other than the Employment Insurance Act, the number that corresponds to that maximum number of weeks".
-- src:2467 | — 2009, c. 30, s. 7
-- src:2468 | Subsection 55(10) of regulations
-- src:2469 | 7 With respect to a claimant to whom any of sections 3 to 6 applies whose benefit period has not been extended under any of subsections 10(13) to (13.3) of the Employment Insurance Act, subsection 55(10) of the Employment Insurance Regulations is deemed to read as follows:
-- src:2470 | (10)In a claimant’s benefit period, a claim- ant who is not in Canada or a claimant referred to in subsection (8), subject to the applicable maximums set out in paragraphs (7)(a) and (b), may combine the weeks of benefits to which the claimant is entitled, but the total number of weeks of benefits shall not exceed 50 or, if the maximum number of weeks during which benefits may be paid to a claimant under section 225 of the Budget Implementation Act, 2009 is equal to or greater than 50 weeks as a result of the application of any provision of any Act of Parliament, other than the Employment Insurance Act, the number that corresponds to that maximum number of weeks.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations, Related Provisions, 2009, c. 30, s. 7 (src:2467-2470)
GIVEN `any of sections 3 to 6 applies to the claimant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the benefit period has been extended under any of subsections 10(13) to (13.3) of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN   -- out of range: s 10 (piece ei1)
      `the claimant is not in Canada or is a claimant referred to in subsection 55(8)` IS A BOOLEAN   -- out of range: reg 55(8) (piece er3)
      `the maximum number of weeks during which benefits may be paid to the claimant under section 225 of the Budget Implementation Act, 2009 as a result of any provision of an Act of Parliament other than the Employment Insurance Act` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Regs related provision 2009 c 30 s 7 the greatest total number of weeks of benefits that may be combined` IS
    IF     `any of sections 3 to 6 applies to the claimant`
       AND NOT (`the benefit period has been extended under any of subsections 10(13) to (13.3) of the Act`)
       AND `the claimant is not in Canada or is a claimant referred to in subsection 55(8)`
    THEN JUST (IF `the maximum number of weeks during which benefits may be paid to the claimant under section 225 of the Budget Implementation Act, 2009 as a result of any provision of an Act of Parliament other than the Employment Insurance Act` AT LEAST 50
               THEN `the maximum number of weeks during which benefits may be paid to the claimant under section 225 of the Budget Implementation Act, 2009 as a result of any provision of an Act of Parliament other than the Employment Insurance Act`
               ELSE 50)
    ELSE NOTHING

§ `SOR/2012-260 ss. 4 and 5 -- which version of subsection 55(4) and of subsection 55.01(3) governs`

DECLARE `er6 Version of a provision of the Regulations` IS ONE OF
    `er6 the version that read immediately before December 9, 2012`
    `er6 the version enacted by the amending regulations`

-- s 4(1) and (2) say one thing from the two sides: the new subsection 55(4) does not apply, and the old one continues to apply, to a
-- claimant whose benefit period was established before December 9, 2012. NOTHING: the provision does not speak (the person is not one referred to in 55(4)).
-- src:2472 | — SOR/2012-260, s. 4
-- src:2473 | 4 (1) Subsection 55(4) of the Employment Insurance Regulations, as enacted by section 1, does not apply in respect of a claimant referred to in that subsection whose benefit period was established before December 9, 2012.
-- src:2474 | (2) Subsection 55(4) of the Employment Insurance Regulations, as it read immediately before December 9, 2012, continues to apply in respect of a claimant referred to in that subsection whose benefit period was established before that day.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations, Related Provisions, SOR/2012-260 s. 4 (src:2472-2474)
GIVEN `is a claimant referred to in subsection 55(4)` IS A BOOLEAN   -- out of range: reg 55(4) (piece er3)
      `the day on which the benefit period was established` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE `er6 Version of a provision of the Regulations`
DECIDE `Regs related provision SOR/2012-260 s 4 the version of subsection 55(4) that governs` IS
    IF NOT (`is a claimant referred to in subsection 55(4)`)
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF `the day on which the benefit period was established` LESS THAN YearMonthDay 2012 12 9
         THEN JUST `er6 the version that read immediately before December 9, 2012`
         ELSE JUST `er6 the version enacted by the amending regulations`

-- src:2476 | — SOR/2012-260, s. 5
-- src:2477 | 5 (1) Subsection 55.01(3) of the Employment Insurance Regulations, as enacted by section 2, does not apply in respect of a self-employed person referred to in that subsection whose benefit period was established before December 9, 2012.
-- src:2478 | (2) Subsection 55.01(3) of the Employment Insurance Regulations, as it read immediately before December 9, 2012, continues to apply in respect of a self-employed person referred to in that subsection whose benefit period was established before that day.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations, Related Provisions, SOR/2012-260 s. 5 (src:2476-2478)
GIVEN `is a self-employed person referred to in subsection 55.01(3)` IS A BOOLEAN   -- out of range: reg 55.01(3) (piece er3)
      `the day on which the benefit period was established` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE `er6 Version of a provision of the Regulations`
DECIDE `Regs related provision SOR/2012-260 s 5 the version of subsection 55.01(3) that governs` IS
    IF NOT (`is a self-employed person referred to in subsection 55.01(3)`)
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF `the day on which the benefit period was established` LESS THAN YearMonthDay 2012 12 9
         THEN JUST `er6 the version that read immediately before December 9, 2012`
         ELSE JUST `er6 the version enacted by the amending regulations`

§ `2022, c. 10, s. 350.1 -- continued application, before September 25, 2022`

-- (2) the definitions: "new Regulations" are the Regulations as they read on September 25, 2022; "former Regulations" as they read immediately before it.
-- src:2483 | Definitions
-- src:2484 | (2) The following definitions apply in this section.
-- src:2485 | claimant has the same meaning as in subsection 2(1) of the Employment Insurance Act. (prestataire)
-- src:2486 | earnings means the earnings referred to in subsections 36(9) and (10) of the new Regulations. (rémunération)
-- src:2487 | former Regulations means the Employment Insurance Regulations as they read immediately before September 25, 2022. (ancien règlement)
-- src:2488 | new Regulations means the Employment Insurance Regulations as they read on September 25, 2022. (nouveau règlement)
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations, Related Provisions, 2022, c. 10, s. 350.1(2) (src:2483-2488)
`Regs related provision 2022 c 10 s 350.1(2) the day on which the new Regulations are read` MEANS YearMonthDay 2022 9 25

@ref Employment Insurance Regulations, Related Provisions, 2022, c. 10, s. 350.1(2) (src:2487)
`Regs related provision 2022 c 10 s 350.1(2) the last day on which the former Regulations read` MEANS
    `Regs related provision 2022 c 10 s 350.1(2) the day on which the new Regulations are read` MINUS 1

@ref Employment Insurance Regulations, Related Provisions, 2022, c. 10, s. 350.1(2) (src:2485)
`Regs related provision 2022 c 10 s 350.1(1) the period in which the first week of the weeks of allocation must fall` MEANS
    `Period of days` WITH
        `first day of the period` IS YearMonthDay 2021 9 26
        `last day of the period` IS YearMonthDay 2022 9 24

-- (1) "continue to apply in respect of a claimant's earnings if, but for this subsection, the earnings would be allocated under subsection 36(9) or (10) of the new
-- Regulations to a number of weeks the first week of which falls within the period beginning on September 26, 2021 and ending on September 24, 2022."
-- src:2480 | — 2022, c. 10, s. 350.1
-- src:2481 | Continued application — before September 25, 2022
-- src:2482 | 350.1 (1) Subsection 35(6), paragraph 35(7)(g) and section 36 of the former Regulations continue to apply in respect of a claimant’s earnings if, but for this subsection, the earnings would be allocated under subsection 36(9) or (10) of the new Regulations to a number of weeks the first week of which falls within the period beginning on September 26, 2021 and ending on September 24, 2022.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations, Related Provisions, 2022, c. 10, s. 350.1(1) (src:2480-2482)
GIVEN `applies for benefits under the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `has applied for benefits under the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the earnings would be allocated under subsection 36(9) or (10) of the new Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN   -- out of range: reg 36(9) and (10) (piece er3)
      `the first week of the weeks to which they would be allocated begins on` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Regs related provision 2022 c 10 s 350.1(1) subsection 35(6), paragraph 35(7)(g) and section 36 of the former Regulations continue to apply to the claimant’s earnings` IF
        `s 2(1) claimant` `applies for benefits under the Act` `has applied for benefits under the Act`
    AND `the earnings would be allocated under subsection 36(9) or (10) of the new Regulations`
    AND `the day` `the first week of the weeks to which they would be allocated begins on` `falls within` `Regs related provision 2022 c 10 s 350.1(1) the period in which the first week of the weeks of allocation must fall`
